C.2 Optimal Aperture Distribution via KKT Conditions

We minimise total cost $C = c_1 \sum_i A_i^\kappa + C_{\text{FF}}$ subject to fixed total area $\sum_i A_i = A_{\text{tot}}$, ignoring the weak dependence of $C_{\text{FF}}$ on $A_i$ through baseline length (which we treat as fixed for a given formation geometry). The Lagrangian is

\mathcal{L} = c_1 \sum_i A_i^\kappa - \lambda \Bigl(\sum_i A_i - A_{\text{tot}}\Bigr).

Stationarity $\partial \mathcal{L}/\partial A_i = c_1 \kappa A_i^{\kappa-1} - \lambda = 0$ yields $A_i = (\lambda/(c_1\kappa))^{1/(\kappa-1)}$, identical for all $i$. Thus uniform distribution is optimal. When formation‑flying costs depend on individual node positions, a small perturbation $A_i^* = A_{\text{tot}}/N + \epsilon_i$ can be optimised; the correction $\epsilon_i$ is of order $\mathcal{O}( \frac{\partial C_{\text{FF}}}{\partial A_i} / \kappa )$, which is negligible for our parameters. Hence the uniform allocation is adopted.

