E.3 Optimal Baseline Length Derivation

Maximising $\beta \log L - \gamma C_{\text{FF}}(L)$ with $C_{\text{FF}} \propto L^\nu$ gives the first‑order condition

\frac{\beta}{L} - \gamma \nu c_4 N \frac{L^{\nu-1}}{L_0^\nu} \Bigl(\frac{\sigma_{\text{piston}}}{\sigma_0}\Bigr)^{-\mu} = 0
\;\Rightarrow\;
L_{\text{opt}} = \left( \frac{\beta}{\gamma \nu c_4 N} \right)^{1/\nu} L_0 \Bigl(\frac{\sigma_{\text{piston}}}{\sigma_0}\Bigr)^{\mu/\nu}.

Plugging in $\beta=1$, $\gamma=10^{-3}$ (to balance units), $c_4=45.6$ M$, $\nu=1.18$, $N=4$, $\sigma_{\text{piston}}=1$ nm, $L_0=100$ km, yields $L_{\text{opt}} \approx 55$ km, consistent with the chosen 50 km.

