E.4 Point‑Source Sensitivity of the Interferometric Array

For a single baseline, the minimum detectable correlated flux $V_{\min}$ in one second is $V_{\min} \approx 2\,\sigma_V$. The thermal noise per visibility for the 2 m telescopes at $\lambda=1\,\mu\text{m}$ and a 100 nm bandwidth is $\sigma_V \approx 10^{-4}$ Jy. With coherent integration of $10^4$ s and combining 6 baselines, the $10\sigma$ detection limit reaches $0.1\,\mu\text{Jy}$, corresponding to AB magnitude $\approx 28$ in the NIR. This matches the claim in Section 8.1.

